  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "biz-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Business workspace, redrawn from the captures in ../screenshots (2026-08-22).\nTop row: mobile, 390x844. Bottom row: desktop, 1440x900 — a centred 1232px column under a fixed top bar, with tracking splitting into map + a 318px right rail.\nMaps are placeholders; the real screens render MapLibre + OpenStreetMap tiles, which cannot load inside an artboard.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "biz-desk-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1960,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Desktop tracking keeps the nav on Request, not a tab of its own — the rail replaces the phone's bottom sheet and carries the same content in the same order.",
      "page": "page-1"
    },
    {
      "id": "rider-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Courier workspace. The order's value appears nowhere on this side: GET /api/trips nulls orderPrice for the rider, so a price on a courier screen would be a bug.\nEvery action screen states its own gate in plain words — 235 m to go, confirm within 31 m — because the server refuses the button otherwise.",
      "page": "page-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "rider-desk-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1960,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "The courier app has no desktop layout of its own. On a wide screen the same phone column is centred on the shell colour, so it reads as a device against a desk. Captured, not assumed: ../screenshots/desktop/rider-*.png.",
      "page": "page-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "entry-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Landing and sign-in. The red brand panel is the one place the marketing voice shows up; everything past sign-in is the workspace.",
      "page": "page-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "lofi-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -190,
      "w": 760,
      "text": "Lo-fi wireframes: structure and the rule each screen has to honour, before any styling.",
      "page": "page-4"
    }
  ],
